.TH pwd 1 "FUZIX System Utilities" "FUZIX"
.SH NAME
pwd \- print the working directory
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B pwd
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B pwd
writes the absolute path of the current working directory.
.SH OPTIONS
None.
.SH EXIT STATUS
1, with a message, if the path cannot be determined \- which generally
means a directory above the current one has been removed, or is not
readable.
.SH NOTES
The shell has its own
.B pwd
built in;
.B /bin/pwd
is what a script gets when it runs the command by path, and what
.BR ssh (1)
runs.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR sh (1),
.BR ls (1)
